  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi alloy has low friction and wear at room temperature.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The friction and wear of unmodified CoCrFeNi increase at elevated temperatures.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A functionally graded, nanostructured coating can maintain low friction and reduced wear on CoCrFeNi from room temperature through 800 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Functional grading of the coating can tailor oxidation kinetics to produce a stable lubricious oxide layer at temperatures of at least 600 °C.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coating can remain chemically and mechanically inert at room temperature.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The graded compositional and microstructural interface enables controlled tribo-oxidation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The graded nanostructure optimizes the coating's mechanical response across the full temperature range.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperature, frictional heating promotes oxidation of the coating by atmospheric oxygen.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-temperature tribo-oxidation forms a thin, continuous lubricious oxide glaze.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide glaze reduces friction and protects against adhesive and abrasive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "At room temperature, an inert coating phase prevents premature oxidation and preserves the starting alloy's low-friction behavior.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coated alloy will have lower coefficients of friction and lower wear rates than unmodified CoCrFeNi throughout the entire room-temperature-to-800 °C range.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coating's largest improvement over unmodified CoCrFeNi will occur above 600 °C, where the oxide glaze becomes active.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed operating boundary is sliding in ambient air at approximately 25–800 °C, under normal loads of approximately 5–30 N and sliding speeds of 1–5 mm/s.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The long-term stability of the proposed oxide glaze under cyclic thermal and mechanical loading is uncertain.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prolonged cyclic shear can fragment a protective oxide film into abrasive debris and accelerate material loss.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
